  "atoms": [
    {
      "id": "a0",
      "pos": 1,
      "text": "Consequentialism holds that the moral status of an act depends solely on its outcomes.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "pos": 2,
      "text": "Deontological theories hold that some acts are wrong irrespective of the consequences they produce.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "pos": 3,
      "text": "The doctrine of double effect distinguishes effects that are intended from effects that are merely foreseen.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "pos": 4,
      "text": "The doctrine of double effect permits the causing of a foreseen harm that is not intended.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "pos": 5,
      "text": "The doctrine of double effect permits a harmful effect to be intended as a means to a good end.",
      "factual": false,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5",
      "pos": 6,
      "text": "Thomas Aquinas gave the earliest formulation of the doctrine of double effect in his discussion of self-defence in the Summa Theologiae.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6",
      "pos": 7,
      "text": "Philippa Foot introduced the trolley case in a 1967 paper on abortion and the doctrine of double effect.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a7",
      "pos": 8,
      "text": "Trolley cases are constructed to isolate the moral relevance of intention from the moral relevance of outcomes.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8",
      "pos": 9,
      "text": "The method of reflective equilibrium tests general moral principles against considered judgments about particular cases.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9",
      "pos": 10,
      "text": "Re A concerned conjoined twins given the names Jodie and Mary.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a10",
      "pos": 11,
      "text": "The surgeons' purpose in operating was the preservation of Jodie's life.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a11",
